mary\": \"Multiple drugs are tied to life-threatening arrhythmias and cardiac arrest\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond bradycardia, several agents are connected to more severe cardiac events. For instance, 酒石酸美托洛尔缓释片II is associated with 室性心动过速 (ventricular tachycardia), particularly upon abrupt discontinuation in coronary artery disease patients [Data: Relationships (16460)]. Meanwhile, 心脏停搏 (cardiac arrest) is flagged as a critical outcome linked to symptom clusters including 呼吸急促 (tachypnea) [Data: Relationships (18030)]. These relationships illustrate a continuum of cardiac risk—from rhythm disturbances to fatal outcomes—associated with commonly used cardiovascular and other systemic medications.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug-induced liver injury emerges as a significant hepatic safety concern\",\n            \"explanation\": \"药物性肝损伤 (drug-induced liver injury) is documented in association with antiviral regimens like 雷迪帕韦/索磷布韦, particularly in HIV/HCV co-infected patients on concomitant antiretroviral therapy (e.g., LPV/r) [Data: Relationships (18598)]. A key biomarker, 胆红素升高 (elevated bilirubin), appears both as a symptom of drug-induced liver injury and as a direct adverse effect of compounds like 姜黄素 when combined with bioenhancers such as piperine [Data: Relationships (18598, 11255)]. This dual pathway underscores the liver’s vulnerability to metabolic competition and highlights bilirubin monitoring as essential in polypharmacy involving hepatobiliary-clearance drugs.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Systemic anesthesia and antibiotic combinations pose neuromuscular risks\",\n            \"explanation\": \"全身麻醉药 (general anesthetics) interact dangerously with 氨基糖苷类抗生素 (aminoglycoside antibiotics), potentiating neuromuscular blockade and risking respiratory paralysis [Data: Relationships (29718)]. Although this relationship involves entities not central to the core cardiovascular cluster, it reflects broader patterns of high-severity drug–drug interactions within the dataset. This finding reinforces the need for anesthetic and antimicrobial stewardship, especially in surgical or critically ill patients receiving multiple CNS-depressant or neuromuscular-blocking agents.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community exhibits high impact severity due to multiple documented links between widely used drugs and life-threatening adverse reactions, including cardiac arrest, fatal bradycardia, and drug-induced liver injury.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782126392, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1483, "prompt_tokens": 6951, "total_tokens": 8434, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Cardiovascular and Hepatic Drug Safety Community: Focus on 雷迪帕韦/索磷布韦, 丙吡胺, and 胺碘达隆\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on a network of drugs (including 雷迪帕韦/索磷布韦, 丙吡胺, 胺碘达隆, 伊伐布雷定, 米力农, and others), symptoms (notably 心动过缓, 室性心动过速, 心脏停搏), and serious adverse effects such as 死亡 and 药物性肝损伤. Key relationships highlight clinically significant drug–adverse reaction links, contraindications in specific populations (e.g., 肾功能欠佳患者), and symptom clusters associated with cardiac dysfunction. Several drugs are implicated in potentially life-threatening cardiovascular events or hepatic complications, indicating a high-risk pharmacovigilance profile.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"雷迪帕韦/索磷布韦 and 索莫布韦 are linked to bradycardia, especially in combination therapies\",\n            \"explanation\": 